  "id": "higher-order-correlation",
  "term": "higher order correlation",
  "definition": "Higher-order correlation is the simultaneous relationship among more than two sets of variables, such as several types of omics data together with a phenotype. In multi-omics analysis, it is used to capture more complex patterns than simple pairwise correlations and can give a more complete view of how features are connected.",
